# `.github/` decides how every other change is judged: this file names who approves it,
# `workflows/ci.yml` publishes the check the `main` ruleset waits for, and a `dependabot.yml` added
# later decides which dependency updates open themselves. The rule above already reaches all of it,
# so this entry changes no ownership today. It states that ownership deliberately rather than by
# inheritance, which is what the last-matching-pattern rule makes worth writing down: whoever adds a
# path rule under `.github/` later sees the requirement it has to keep, instead of discovering it
# from a review that no longer asks for the owner. The `Protected paths` check refuses the same
# change from the other side, before a reviewer is involved.
